$ grep -n UAT-008 -A6 /Users/johnyang/code/verdi-system/docs/design/uat/uat-findings.md | head -8
47:| UAT-008 | artifact contract | docs | low | open | 02 says `status` required; decoder accepts a statusless proposal |
48-| UAT-009 | artifact contract | contract | medium | open | Constraints and open questions cannot carry `links:` |
49-| UAT-010 | stubs | contract | medium | open | Story stubs cannot claim open questions; stub-match is exact-set and slug-equal |
50-| UAT-011 | zones / worktrees | contract | low | open | CLI lint inside a Verdi-managed design worktree can never see the mutable zone |
51-| UAT-012 | store compatibility | plausible | low | open | Older build rejects `.verdi/imports` written by a newer build (VL-007); no store version stamp |
52-| UAT-017 | readiness / acceptance | contract | high | fixed pending merge | Every declared open question blocks acceptance even when a spike stub claims it; 02 allows accepted features with spike-resolved questions |
53-| UAT-018 | policy / adoption | defect | medium | fixed pending merge | Adopting Verdi establishes no policy authority; every board then carries an unproven policy item with a manual setup guide, and semantic review is refused |
